                <pb facs="0444" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1199a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-13T00:00:00-04:00">December 13,
                            1943—midnight.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1365. Your 3908, December 2. Please inform the Foreign Minister that this
                    Government has read with much gratification the text of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> made to the German Minister at Stockholm
                    on the occasion of this further instance of barbaric and inhuman action by
                    Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
